# harness.config — fill these in after pasting the harness into a project.
#
# A few skills reference things only your project knows: where its packages live, which
# cloud project it deploys to, which chat channel your team talks in. Those were stripped
# before publishing and replaced by {{VARS}}. Copy this file to `harness.config`, fill in
# what applies, then run:
#
#   ./fill-vars.sh /path/to/project harness.config
#
# Anything you leave out stays as a visible {{VAR}} and gets reported, so nothing is
# silently blanked. Delete the lines that make no sense for your stack.
#
# `harness.config` is gitignored. Never commit the filled-in version.

# ── Where things live ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PROJECT_ROOT=/Users/you/Projects/my-app

# Monorepo package path used by the merge skill (locale output vs locale input).
# Single-package repo? Drop it.
PKG_ADMIN=packages/admin                 # admin/dashboard frontend

# ── Git ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
GIT_REMOTE_HOST=git.example.com/org/repo

# ── Cloud projects ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used only to describe how a deployed bundle is polled to detect which branch a
# staging environment is actually running. Skills append -N for numbered stagings.
FIREBASE_STAGING=my-app-staging

# ── Team channels ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DEV_CHANNEL=dev                          # chat channel the catch-up skill reads

# ── Deliberately absent ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No store domains, no test logins, no mailbox credentials. The skill that needed
# them (which tenant belongs to which app, how to read a real inbox for a one-time
# code) is not published here at all: that is a description of one company's estate,
# and variable-substitution does not make it safe to ship. Keep yours in a private
# repo alongside the rest of your product-specific skills.
